Same-card subscriber identity planning (local research modifications,
2026-10-26): independently written EC20 AT+CIMI / EF_IMSI observations with
before-and-after source checks, bounded per-ICCID private identity history,
successful-IMS priority and legal-home plans. Wire EAP/SIP use the chosen
identity; AKA and incoming business callbacks retain the physical reader
identity. A precise, cleaned-up identity-only EAP rejection can permit the
next candidate, never a challenge, malformed exchange, backoff or failed
cleanup. Native QMI live multi-source support and real carrier/multi-modem
acceptance remain incomplete. Tests use synthetic SIMs, encrypted transcripts,
loopback SIP and file-backed SQLite on root@10.0.0.2, not WSL or live services.
No protocol source is copied across licenses and no dependency is added.
Original LICENSE and regional/device/SIM authorization controls are unchanged.

